{"id":"q60","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"fact","question":"Is a strawberry a berry in the botanical sense?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"A strawberry is fleshy, sweet, and has many small seeds on its surface, resembling the everyday idea of a berry.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.3,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Some botanists loosely treat the strawberry as a berry-like fruit.","confidence":0.5,"lean":0.2,"theta":0.7854,"phi":0.0},{"text":"A botanical true berry develops from a single ovary, with the whole ovary wall becoming fleshy and seeds embedded inside.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"A strawberry's edible flesh is mostly swollen receptacle tissue, not ovary wall.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The small hard seed-like structures on the outside of a strawberry are the true fruits, which are achenes.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"A strawberry is an accessory fruit built from receptacle tissue around achenes.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Tissue origin is the deciding factor in whether a fruit is a botanical berry.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.6,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The strawberry does not meet the botanical definition of a berry.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Fleshy texture and seed arrangement are real similarities but do not define a botanical berry.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":8,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":4,"